addrmap hi3535 {
    name = "hi3535 registers";
    desc = "
## Status

Register map of the Hi3535 (H.264 NVR codec processor: dual Cortex-A9, 2x GbE with TOE, PCIe, SATA 3.0, USB 3.0 and USB 2.0, VDP/HDMI, IVE, MDU). Everything below is taken from the HiSilicon Hi3535 H.264 codec processor user guide / data sheet (Issue 00B08, 2014-02-25, Chinese): the address map (table 1-2), the interrupt table (table 3-25) and the register tables of chapters 2 to 13.
The register blocks were extracted programmatically from the data sheet text (names, offsets, bit ranges, access, reset values; descriptions translated to English) and are labelled PROVEN (data sheet table). Blocks with the same layout as on the Hi3520D reuse the shared blocks in rdl/common (compared register by register, see docs/rdl-campaign/hi3535-datasheet.md of the workspace); where the data sheet differs from the Hi3520D (CRG, MISC, DDRC, IO, AIO, SATA ...) chip-local blocks were generated.
Not modelled because the data sheet has no register tables: HDMI, L2 cache controller, ARM debug, VDH/JPGE/JPGD/TDE/VPSS/VGS/VENC/DDRT/SCD registers, the Audio codec.
Nothing was verified on hardware.

## Addresses

| Start Address | End Address | Description | Documented Here |
|---------------|-------------|-------------|-----------------|
| 0x00000000 | 0x03FFFFFF | Address remapping window: points to the BOOTROM until remapping is cleared, then to the on-chip RAM; 64 MB | &#10060; |
| 0x04000000 | 0x0400FFFF | BOOTROM address space (4 KB actual); 64 KB | &#10060; |
| 0x04010000 | 0x0401FFFF | On-chip RAM address space (10 KB actual); 64 KB | &#10060; |
| 0x10000000 | 0x1000FFFF | NANDC registers; 64 KB | &#9989; NANDC (reused common block) |
| 0x10010000 | 0x1001FFFF | SFC registers; 64 KB | &#9989; SFC (reused common block) |
| 0x10030000 | 0x1003FFFF | USB OHCI registers; 64 KB | &#9989; OHCI (generated from the data sheet) |
| 0x10040000 | 0x1004FFFF | USB EHCI registers; 64 KB | &#9989; EHCI (reused common block) |
| 0x10050000 | 0x1005FFFF | CIPHER registers; 64 KB | &#9989; CIPHER (reused common block) |
| 0x10060000 | 0x1006FFFF | DMAC registers; 64 KB | &#10060; |
| 0x12000000 | 0x1200FFFF | USB 3.0 registers; 64 KB | &#9989; USB3 (generated from the data sheet) |
| 0x12010000 | 0x1201FFFF | SATA 3.0 registers; 64 KB | &#9989; SATA, SATA_PORT (generated from the data sheet) |
| 0x12020000 | 0x1203FFFF | TOE registers (GMAC and TOE); 128 KB | &#9989; TOE (generated from the data sheet) |
| 0x20000000 | 0x2000FFFF | Timer0 registers; 64 KB | &#9989; TIMER0, TIMER1 (reused common block) |
| 0x20010000 | 0x2001FFFF | Timer1 registers; 64 KB | &#9989; TIMER2, TIMER3 (reused common block) |
| 0x20030000 | 0x2003FFFF | CRG registers; 64 KB | &#9989; CRG (generated from the data sheet) |
| 0x20040000 | 0x2004FFFF | WDG registers; 64 KB | &#9989; WDG (reused common block) |
| 0x20050000 | 0x2005FFFF | SYS_CTRL registers; 64 KB | &#9989; SYS_CTRL (generated from the data sheet) |
| 0x20060000 | 0x2006FFFF | RTC registers; 64 KB | &#9989; RTC (reused common block) |
| 0x20070000 | 0x2007FFFF | IR registers; 64 KB | &#9989; IR (reused common block) |
| 0x20080000 | 0x2008FFFF | UART0 registers; 64 KB | &#9989; UART0 (reused common block) |
| 0x20090000 | 0x2009FFFF | UART1 registers; 64 KB | &#9989; UART1 (reused common block) |
| 0x200A0000 | 0x200AFFFF | UART2 registers; 64 KB | &#9989; UART2 (reused common block) |
| 0x200B0000 | 0x200BFFFF | UART3 registers; 64 KB | &#9989; UART3 (reused common block) |
| 0x200D0000 | 0x200DFFFF | I2C registers; 64 KB | &#9989; I2C (reused common block) |
| 0x200E0000 | 0x200EFFFF | PWM registers; 64 KB | &#9989; PWM (generated from the data sheet) |
| 0x200F0000 | 0x200F7FFF | Pin multiplexing registers; 32 KB | &#9989; IOMUX, IOPAD (generated from the data sheet) |
| 0x200F0800 | 0x200FFFFF | Pin control (drive strength) registers; 32 KB | &#9989; IOPAD (generated from the data sheet) |
| 0x20100000 | 0x2010FFFF | HDMI registers; 64 KB | &#10060; |
| 0x20110000 | 0x2011FFFF | DDRC registers; 64 KB | &#9989; DDRC_AXI, DDRC_DMC, DDRC_MUX, DDRC_PHY (generated from the data sheet) |
| 0x20120000 | 0x2012FFFF | MISC registers; 64 KB | &#9989; MISC_CTRL (generated from the data sheet) |
| 0x20130000 | 0x2013FFFF | Timer2 registers; 64 KB | &#9989; TIMER4, TIMER5 (reused common block) |
| 0x20140000 | 0x2014FFFF | Timer3 registers; 64 KB | &#9989; TIMER6, TIMER7 (reused common block) |
| 0x20150000 | 0x2022FFFF | GPIO0 to GPIO13 registers; 14 x 64 KB | &#9989; GPIO0, GPIO1, GPIO2, GPIO3, GPIO4, GPIO5 ... (reused common block) |
| 0x20230000 | 0x2023FFFF | GPIO14 registers; 64 KB | &#9989; GPIO14 (reused common block) |
| 0x20300000 | 0x2030FFFF | ARM WDG/timer/GIC and other internal registers; 64 KB | &#10060; |
| 0x20400000 | 0x2051FFFF | ARM DEBUG; 1152 KB (CoreSight debug APB window of the dual Cortex-A9, not described) | &#10060; |
| 0x205C0000 | 0x205CFFFF | VDP registers; 64 KB | &#9989; VDP (generated from the data sheet) |
| 0x205E0000 | 0x205EFFFF | IVE registers; 64 KB | &#9989; IVE (reused common block) |
| 0x20600000 | 0x2060FFFF | VPSS registers; 64 KB | &#10060; |
| 0x20610000 | 0x2061FFFF | TDE registers; 64 KB | &#10060; |
| 0x20620000 | 0x2062FFFF | VENC registers; 64 KB | &#10060; |
| 0x20630000 | 0x2063FFFF | VDH0 registers; 64 KB | &#10060; |
| 0x20650000 | 0x2065FFFF | VDH1 registers; 64 KB | &#10060; |
| 0x20660000 | 0x2066FFFF | JPGE registers; 64 KB | &#10060; |
| 0x20670000 | 0x2067FFFF | JPGD registers; 64 KB | &#10060; |
| 0x20680000 | 0x2068FFFF | AIO registers; 64 KB | &#9989; AIO (generated from the data sheet) |
| 0x206B0000 | 0x206BFFFF | VGS registers; 64 KB | &#10060; |
| 0x206C0000 | 0x206CFFFF | MD (motion detection) registers; 64 KB | &#9989; MDU (reused common block) |
| 0x206D0000 | 0x206DFFFF | DDRT registers; 64 KB | &#10060; |
| 0x20700000 | 0x207FFFFF | L2 cache space; 1 MB | &#10060; |
| 0x20800000 | 0x2080FFFF | PCIe registers; 64 KB | &#9989; PCIE (generated from the data sheet) |
| 0x30000000 | 0x3FFFFFFF | PCIe memory address space; 256 MB | &#10060; |
| 0x40000000 | 0x4FFFFFFF | PCIe configuration address space; 256 MB | &#10060; |
| 0x50000000 | 0x53FFFFFF | NANDC memory space; 64 MB | &#10060; |
| 0x58000000 | 0x5BFFFFFF | SPI flash memory space; 64 MB | &#10060; |
| 0x80000000 | 0xFFFFFFFF | DDR memory space (external DDR devices); 2 GB | &#10060; |

