        <!-- overview:begin -->

        ### Diagrams

        ![Logic block diagram](assets/diagrams/hi3535-logic.svg)

        ![Register blocks by function](assets/diagrams/hi3535-blocks.svg)

        ![Boot flow](assets/diagrams/hi3535-boot.svg)

        ### Key specifications (data sheet chapter 1; the data sheet is Chinese, translated)

        | | Hi3535 V100 |
        |---|---|
        | CPU | dual Cortex-A9, up to 1 GHz; 32 KB L1 I + 32 KB L1 D per core, 256 KB L2 |
        | DDR | one 32-bit DDR3 controller, up to 800 MHz, up to 2 GB |
        | Decode | H.264 BP/MP/HP L5.0, MPEG4 SP/ASP, MJPEG/JPEG baseline |
        | Encode | H.264 BP/MP/HP L4.2, MJPEG/JPEG baseline |
        | Performance examples | 5x1080p@30 decode + 1x1080p@30 encode; 9x720p@30 decode + 1x1080p@30 encode; 24xD1@30 decode + 1x1080p@30 encode |
        | Video output | 1 HDMI 1.4, 1 VGA (up to 1920x1200@60), 1 BT.1120, 1 CVBS; three full-screen GUI layers (two HD, one SD) and a 128x128 cursor |
        | Audio | integrated audio codec, 2 I2S (1 in, 1 out), software codecs |
        | Network | 2 gigabit Ethernet (RGMII/RMII/MII, TOE) |
        | Peripherals | 2 SATA 3.0, 1 PCIe 2.0 / SATA 3.0 shared port (RC and endpoint), 4 UART (2 with four wires), IR, I2C, GPIO, 2 USB 2.0 host, 1 USB 3.0 host |
        | Flash | SPI NOR (1/2/4 bit, 2 CS, 32 MB each), 8-bit NAND (SLC/MLC, 1/4/8/24 bit ECC) with NAND boot |
        | On-chip memory | 4 KB BOOTROM, 10 KB SRAM |
        | Package | EDHS-PBGA, 23 x 23 mm, 0.8 mm pitch; 3.5 W typical; core 1.1 V, CPU 1.2 V (down to 1.1 V), I/O 3.3 V, DDR3 1.5 V |

        ### Boot (data sheet 1.3, Table 1-1)

        | BOOTROM_SEL | BOOT_SEL1 | BOOT_SEL0 | Boot mode |
        |---|---|---|---|
        | 1 | X | X | BOOTROM (serial download) |
        | 0 | 0 | 0 | external SPI flash |
        | 0 | 1 | 0 | external NAND flash |
        | 0 | 0 | 1 | slave mode: the CPU does not start; a master chip loads the boot program into this chip's DDR over PCIe and releases its reset |

        BOOTROM_SEL is multiplexed with pin MDCK, BOOT_SEL1 with VOU1120_DATA10 and BOOT_SEL0 with VOU1120_DATA7. With BOOTROM_SEL = 1 the BOOTROM starts the serial download; if the serial link times out it evaluates BOOT_SEL1/BOOT_SEL0 (00 = SPI flash, 10 = NAND flash).

